N5008 [over.match.copy]/1.1, [class.conv.ctor]/2: in copy-initialization
`E e = 1;' only converting (non-explicit) constructors are candidates, so
the program is ill-formed.  The front end accepts it (also through class
template argument deduction, `template <class T> struct E { explicit E(T);
}; E e = 1;').  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 reject this
program.
